      ],
      "text": "**For a short trip or commute, an N95 usually isn’t necessary—but for a long time outdoors, I’d wear a well-fitting N95, KN95, FFP2 or KF94, and skip strenuous outdoor exercise.**\n\nSingapore’s haze was **unhealthy to very unhealthy on October 16**. At 8pm, hourly PM2.5 was elevated in most regions, though the latest reading can change—check your area’s live NEA reading before heading out. Older adults, pregnant people, and anyone with heart or lung conditions should avoid outdoor activity when PM2.5 is high. ([channelnewsasia.com](https://www.channelnewsasia.com/singapore/haze-oct-16-psi-pm-25-6459416))\n\nIf you have breathing trouble or the haze bothers you, head indoors; a mask doesn’t make prolonged outdoor exertion a good idea. ([channelnewsasia.com](https://www.channelnewsasia.com/singapore/haze-oct-16-psi-pm-25-6459416))",
